title Fold AA -- post_the_amendment, and the price was one word
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds first, one council-rota doc deep-read, send the increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. crux/REDS.md carries no row marked OPEN; the ledger stands at 110 rows, every one closed on a witness. No red preempts constructive work this lap.
think Council rota, lap index 589 kyri logs mod 27 -> item 22, context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md. Deep-read. Its law lands squarely on this arc: an idea is truly held only when it can be rebuilt from your own materials. A fold is that test applied to code -- thirty-five rungs each holding the same forty-five lines were repeating a saying rather than owning it, and lifting the body into one text that speaks through the rung handed in is the same act, in Rye.
think The running thread from fold Z named the crux by measurement: post_the_amendment at 35 rungs by 45 lines, 1530 carried, with run_dependent at 43 by 35 behind it. Hash the family before trusting the count -- the discipline this arc has earned three separate ways.
think Hashing every post_the_amendment on the ladder found thirty-six, not thirty-five. The thirty-sixth is amend.rye, and its diff is the second kind of absentee exactly: where the cohort reaches its report through amending_of(report_out), the tier owner reaches report_out directly, because the amending report is its report. Confirmed by grep -- amend.rye has no amending_of at all. It stays home; the cohort is thirty-five.
think Fold Z's lesson applied before choosing scope: read the reach closure first. The body reaches sixteen symbols. Fifteen already stood public in all thirty-five, interest paid by the folds before this one. Only amending_of was private, in twenty-seven of the thirty-five.
think Then the second half of that lesson -- does the widened helper fold with the body? Hashing amending_of across the cohort found thirty-five distinct texts, one per rung, each a different depth of .inner. It is an identity accessor by construction and folds nowhere, exactly as fold R's rule predicts. So the fold costs twenty-seven widenings and births no accessor.
think Wrote the harness body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye reaching everything through the rung handed in, replaced thirty-five bodies with three-line delegates, widened amending_of in twenty-seven files, then repinned the meter and its ceiling.
obs The arithmetic closes with no remainder and was measured rather than predicted: thirty-four copies of forty-five in at 1,530, thirty-four copies of three out at 102, fall 1,428, and the meter read 114,189 -> 112,761 exactly. Carrying families stand unmoved at 706 -- one family out and one back in -- because unlike fold Z there was no visibility split to heal.
obs The lesson this lap adds is about price rather than shape. Twenty-six folds in, a family of thirty-five reached fifteen already-public symbols. A fold pays its widenings once and every fold after inherits them, so the ladder is now mostly paid and the folds ahead are mostly free. What still costs is the reading -- hash the family, audit the reach, name the absentee -- and that reading has never once been wasted.
obs Repinning the meter meant freshening three prose lines that recited fold Z's cluster. A witness that narrates a lap it no longer measures is a stale claim wearing a witness's clothes; the numbers live in the asserts and the scan output, and the prose says only what this lap did.
